Atelier's components include a document-ingestion pipeline, vector store, retrieval layer with hybrid search, orchestration layer, and answer layer. This model-agnostic platform can be containerized using Kubernetes, ensuring flexibility and scalability. Our architecture and integration capabilities include API-first design with REST and webhook, support for HL7 and FHIR through our health interoperability capabilities, and standard connectors for SIH and DPI integration.

To meet the client's requirements, we will integrate Atelier with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI), leveraging our partnerships with Ligeo Santé for delivery and OuraneCloud for hosting. Our Sovereign HDS tier infrastructure is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and hosted on EU-only, renewable-powered infrastructure, ensuring data sovereignty and compliance with regulatory requirements.

In terms of performance, Atelier has a median latency of 1.3 seconds, common queries p95 latency below 2 seconds, and complex multi-source synthesis queries p95 latency below 2.5 seconds. We expect to achieve high availability, targeting 99.9%, to support continuity of care. Our hosting options include the Sovereign HDS tier, which meets the HDS certification requirement and utilizes renewable energy.

Our company holds ISO 27001 certification since 2023, covering development, delivery, and operations, demonstrating our commitment to information security management. We also comply with the Health Data Hosting (HDS) certification through our hosting infrastructure operated on OuraneCloud. To protect sensitive data, we employ encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, as well as pseudonymisation, data minimization, and configurable retention.

As a Société par actions simplifiée registered in France, we have up-to-date social and fiscal obligations and administrative attestations available, including those required for French public procurement. Our intellectual property model is based on proprietary software licensed to clients under a subscription or usage model, and we use permissive open-source licenses for open-source components.

The client's budget of €900,000 over 5 years translates to an average annual budget of €180,000. Our standard daily rates for various roles are between €700 and €1,300, providing flexibility in staffing the project without exceeding the budget. With our Series A funding of €12,000,000 raised in 2024, we have a comfortable cash runway and a solid financial foundation.

Our RAG approach grounds answers in the client's controlled corpus, ensuring explainability and traceability. We can leverage this capability to provide contextualization, drafting assistance, and support for medical coding (PMSI, ICD-10) while demonstrating explainability and transparency. Our system provides source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval traces, and logs every interaction for posterior audit.

As a responsible business, we prioritize sustainability and have an EcoVadis rating of Silver. We partner with green hosting providers like OuraneCloud in the EU, which uses renewable energy and has a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2. We practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching, and we are committed to reducing our carbon intensity per managed assistant year on year.

Our ethics charter includes principles such as human oversight, transparency, bias monitoring, data minimization, and a documented data-use policy, aligning with regulatory requirements like the EU AI Act. We believe that our strong CSR and sustainability posture will contribute to sustainable development, while carefully managing trade-offs between high availability and energy consumption.

In conclusion, our consortium is confident in its ability to deliver an AI assistance solution that meets the client's requirements, ensuring decision traceability, explainability, and transparency. With Atelier, we can provide hospital staff with a valuable tool that supports their clinical-administrative activities, while maintaining a robust security and compliance posture, and contributing to sustainable development. We look forward to working with CHRB to improve the efficiency of its staff and the quality and safety of care.
